    <string name="car_info_title">Car Speed Settings</string>
    <string name="car_info_intro">Speed compensation helps keep sound audible over road noise. It has two independent parts: volume and equalizer.</string>
    <string name="car_info_volume_title">Volume (GALA)</string>
    <string name="car_info_volume_text">Raises overall loudness as speed grows from Min Speed to Max Speed, up to Max Boost. Boost is automatically limited if the system volume is already high, so it won\'t clip.</string>
    <string name="car_info_eq_title">Speed Equalizer</string>
    <string name="car_info_eq_text">For each enabled frequency, gain is applied gradually from 0 dB at Min Speed to the set value at Max Speed. 0 dB means "no extra change on top of the preset"; the value is added to the preset\'s own EQ. For example, +3 dB on a bass band adds 3 dB to that band only at higher speed.</string>
