    <!-- FX -->
    <string name="fx_title">FX</string>
    <string name="fx_info_desc">About FX</string>
    <string name="fx_info_text">\"Space\" — two controls:
• \"Width\" — the system Virtualizer (stereo widening; not every device has it). 0% turns it off.
• \"Treble\" — lifts the upper range in the EQ: 1 kHz up to +3 dB, 2–4 kHz up to +5 dB, 8–16 kHz up to +8 dB.

\"Low-Volume Boost\" — two controls:
• \"Strength\" — how much of the ISO 226:2003 equal-loudness correction to apply: at low volume, bass and treble are raised by as much as hearing loses relative to 1 kHz. 100% is the full curve difference, capped at +12 dB.
• \"Threshold\" — the volume step from which there is no boost. The real sound pressure in the cabin is unknown, so the level is estimated from the volume step (the threshold counts as 80 phon).</string>
